<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title"><div class="hero-title"><p class="eyebrow">IMMORTALS CONCIERGE / MACAU</p><h1 id="hero-title">A longevity clinic.<br>A flagship destination.</h1><div class="hero-bottom"><p>A first look at what we could create in Macau.<br>The concept. The space. Four architectural possibilities.</p><div class="hero-explore-links"><a class="round-link tour-entry" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}tour/`}><span>Explore the clinic <small>Six rooms in 360°</small></span><span class="circle" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="hero-vision-link" href="#vision">Explore the vision ↓</a></div></div></div><div class="hero-windows" id="hero-windows" aria-label="Four architectural directions"></div><div class="hero-caption"><span>1,100 m² of possibility</span><span>Macau / City of Dreams</span><span>Visual concept study / 2026</span></div></section>
<section class="vision section-wrap" id="vision"><div class="chapter"><span>01 / THE VISION</span><span>A NEW KIND OF ARRIVAL</span></div><div class="vision-statement reveal"><h2>Make people want<br>to walk in.<br><span>Give them a reason<br>to come back.</span></h2><div class="vision-copy"><p class="lead">A flagship for Immortals Concierge that brings discovery, hospitality and private clinical care into one address.</p><p>Our starting guest is already in Macau. A short resort stay leaves little appetite for a full day of testing. The first encounter should be inviting, memorable and easy to fit into the visit.</p><p>Beyond that public welcome sits a quieter clinic: four private suites, dedicated assessment rooms and a team that brings care to the patient.</p></div></div><div class="principles reveal"><article><span class="small-number">01</span><h3>A public invitation</h3><p>An open, welcoming lounge, a working coffee bar and room for discovery. A place that makes longevity tangible.</p></article><article><span class="small-number">02</span><h3>A private clinical world</h3><p>A discreet appointment entrance. Daylit suites with private showers. Dedicated rooms for equipment-led assessments.</p></article><article><span class="small-number">03</span><h3>A brand people remember</h3><p>The flagship is a physical expression of Immortals. The architecture makes the introduction; the relationship continues through membership.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="space section-wrap" id="space"><div class="chapter"><span>02 / THE SPACE</span><span>THREE WAYS TO ORGANISE THE SAME FOOTPRINT</span></div><div class="section-title reveal"><h2>The footprint is fixed.<br>The possibilities are open.</h2><p>Curved glazing facing the Strip. Generous daylight. Double-height volume. A former private casino, reimagined around a very different kind of visit.</p></div><div class="space-facts reveal"><div><strong>1,100<span> m²</span></strong><p>Reported total footprint</p></div><div><strong>04</strong><p>Permanent window-facing suites</p></div><div><strong>03</strong><p>Dedicated assessment rooms</p></div><div><strong>2.4<span> m</span></strong><p>Main corridor clear-width target</p></div></div>
<div class="layout-stage"><div class="layout-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Choose a layout"><button data-layout="0" class="active" aria-pressed="true"><span>01</span> Club <small>A lounge-led welcome</small></button><button data-layout="1" aria-pressed="false"><span>02</span> Gallery <small>An open discovery floor</small></button><button data-layout="2" aria-pressed="false"><span>03</span> Salon <small>A larger flexible salon</small></button></div><div class="layout-body"><div class="plan-display"><button id="open-plan" aria-label="Enlarge the Club floor plan"><img id="plan-image" src="assets/plan-club.svg" alt="Club layout: four window suites, separate assessments and a lounge-led public floor"><span class="enlarge-label">Explore the full plan <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></button></div><div class="layout-notes" aria-live="polite"><p class="eyebrow" id="plan-number">LAYOUT 01</p><h3 id="plan-title">A lounge-led welcome</h3><p id="plan-description"></p><div id="allocation" class="allocation"></div><p class="tradeoff" id="plan-tradeoff"></p><p class="footnote">Indicative public-space areas, calibrated to the reported footprint. These are concept layouts, not surveyed architectural drawings.</p></div></div></div>
<div class="plan-constants"><h3>What stays in every option</h3><div><p>+ Four daylit suites, each with a private shower</p><p>+ Separate VO₂ max, balance and DEXA rooms</p><p>+ A discreet patient entrance and generous circulation</p><p>+ Retained fire escape, with regular lining around its irregular shape</p><p>+ Conventional HBOT, clinical support and a working coffee bar</p><p>+ A flexible public floor that can evolve with demand</p></div></div></section>
<section id="directions" class="architecture"><div class="section-wrap architecture-intro"><div class="chapter"><span>03 / THE ARCHITECTURE</span><span>FOUR DIRECTIONS / NO PREFERRED OPTION</span></div><div class="section-title reveal"><h2>One ambition.<br>Four different atmospheres.</h2><p>Explore each direction through its public lounge, private suite, entrances and treatment rooms. The architectural language changes. The standard of care and hospitality does not.</p></div><nav class="direction-index" aria-label="Jump to an architectural direction"><a href="#futurism">01 / Fluid</a><a href="#asian">02 / Precise</a><a href="#aman">03 / Composed</a><a href="#milanese">04 / Expressive</a></nav></div><div id="direction-stories"></div></section>
